 # Changelog
+
+## 0.5.19 - 2026-10-23 (local test candidate; unpublished)
+
+- Stage the initial Home behind a loading page until the first shelves,
+  account row and visible artwork settle. Slow providers and artwork have
+  bounded grace periods; the initial page always becomes navigable within
+  eight seconds. Keep existing carousel instances, selection and viewport
+  position when later catalogs or Continue Watching arrive.
+- Restore and verify the supplied `loginWithToken` patch. Exchange the phone's
+  approval credential for the API's device session before saving it. Persist
+  successful login immediately, reject failed exchanges and stale approvals,
+  and clean up separately issued sessions after cancellation.
+- Let VLC discard pictures that are already late at the presentation stage.
+  Keep decoder frame skipping, hurry-up and corrupted-picture output disabled,
+  and preserve the native memory and audio lifetime protections. Add bounded
+  decoder, callback, pickup, upload and swap timing diagnostics for the 1080p
+  report. The firmware 12.7 cause remains a console validation question.
+- Review current EVO and VLC upstream sources. EVO v0.12.5 and the stable
+  VideoLAN 3.0.24 core already match the supplied dependencies. Adapt the
+  newer VLC PS5 v0.6.0 coded/visible picture handling to avoid an intermediate
+  video-output copy, and keep each VP9 input's timestamp and visibility with
+  its delayed hardware output. Preserve resident decoder and buffer policies.
+- Add playback volume on right stick up/down, in five-percent steps, with
+  dead zone, hysteresis, repeat limits, focus-loss recentering, a temporary
+  indicator and saved level. Apply gain to owned decoded PCM. Active HDMI
+  passthrough shows receiver/TV guidance and keeps the saved PCM level.
+  L2/R2 retain subtitle-delay and Downloads-sort controls.
+
+The current test results and remaining PS5 checks are recorded in
+[`docs/LOCAL_0_5_19_VALIDATION.md`](docs/LOCAL_0_5_19_VALIDATION.md).
+The old post-0.5.18 work note describes an earlier source-only snapshot.
+This candidate has not been published or submitted to a store.
+
+Title ID: `PPSA74126`. Native content version: `00.069.000`.
 
